WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.790
(somber guitar chord)

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.960
- My first reaction

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.267
was,

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:07.010
"I'm gonna leave my daughter behind."

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.457
And then my next thought was,

00:00:08.457 --> 00:00:09.950
"I've gotta tell the team."

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.470
- After he told us, I felt,

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:12.303
personally, I felt like

00:00:12.303 --> 00:00:13.620
it was just bigger than basketball.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.553
There's no point of being mad

00:00:14.553 --> 00:00:15.989
on the basketball court,

00:00:15.989 --> 00:00:16.822
when, you know what I mean,

00:00:16.822 --> 00:00:17.655
like there's

00:00:17.655 --> 00:00:18.488
bigger issues.

00:00:18.488 --> 00:00:20.770
- My relationship with the guys,

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.580
I'll never forget 'em.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:23.870
I think one of the things

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.250
they definitely learned this year though

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.300
is that

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.750
we all can't do this by ourselves.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.200
I'm not gonna quit.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.730
I'm gonna be here

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.650
to give my daughter driving lessons,

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.840
walk her down the aisle,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:36.673
all that stuff.

00:00:36.673 --> 00:00:38.420
Death is not a option to me.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.639
I'm not going anywhere.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:42.048
(uplifting synth music)

00:00:42.048 --> 00:00:43.650
(applause)

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:44.570
- Everyone welcome

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.848
Coach Danny O'Fallon, y'all!

00:00:46.848 --> 00:00:49.909
(hooting, applause)

00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:51.440
Whoo!

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.288
You,

00:00:52.288 --> 00:00:53.630
you got me!

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:54.700
Whew!

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.298
Your determination is

00:00:56.298 --> 00:00:57.680
amazing.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.480
Where does it come from?

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.270
- Honestly, it comes from my family.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:02.640
I grew up in an athletic family,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.930
from baseball players

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.060
to basketball players

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.530
and

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:07.400
just

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.260
the fun of playing sports

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.120
and the determination to do your best

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.280
whatever court, field,

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.280
whatever you're on, has

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.420
always been part of our...
- Yeah!

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.420
- Our motto.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.253
- Wow!

00:01:17.253 --> 00:01:18.086
That's why you're an amazing human,

00:01:18.086 --> 00:01:18.919
all right.

00:01:18.919 --> 00:01:20.180
Well, what made you

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.013
have,

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.255
what do you think made you have

00:01:22.255 --> 00:01:23.670
such an exceptional season?

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:24.503
- My team,

00:01:24.503 --> 00:01:26.570
I was fortunate enough to have

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.810
a great group of kids my first year there.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:29.810
When we won the title

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:31.550
was only my second year at the school.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:32.383
- Wow.

00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:34.070
- And I was able to get
a great group of kids

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.060
the first year.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.670
When we lost in the second round

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.060
in the previous year,

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.410
when they came back,

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.410
their determination was just everything.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.290
And, you know,

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:43.460
it was a kind of a situation

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.550
where

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.200
they just didn't want to
take 'no' for an answer.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.280
It just kind of followed suit

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.380
throughout the day.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.810
- How do you think that the team's success

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.230
helped you battle cancer?

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.110
- Our motto,

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:54.390
throughout the year,

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:55.223
has always been,

00:01:55.223 --> 00:01:56.640
"Be about one-and-oh."

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.340
My players are not just players.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.230
They're student-athletes,

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.820
and they understand that
they're students first

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.880
and athletes second.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.713
- Amen, yeah.

00:02:02.713 --> 00:02:03.546
- And,

00:02:03.546 --> 00:02:05.010
so our motto being "one-and-oh,"

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.300
is not just to win the game,

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.940
it's to win the day.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:08.773
And, you know,

00:02:08.773 --> 00:02:10.500
seize the day, seize the moment,

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.940
and even when things like,

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:13.850
situations like cancer get you down,

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.730
you just do your best to battle through,

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.560
and they helped me,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.420
along with my family helped me,

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:21.430
every day, they're all about being

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.263
one-and-oh.

00:02:22.263 --> 00:02:23.096
- Do you think it helps,

00:02:23.096 --> 00:02:23.929
being productive, still,

00:02:23.929 --> 00:02:26.130
and just going on about
your business, so it

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:27.110
doesn't slow you down?
- Oh, yes,

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.890
absolutely, I mean,

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.610
yes, there's days that

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.333
I just can't.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.330
But every chance I get,

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.163
with,

00:02:36.163 --> 00:02:38.350
the love and care from my wife

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:39.183
and my daughter,

00:02:39.183 --> 00:02:40.230
and of course, my guys,

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.330
they're like, "Coach,
you need to be here,"

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:42.357
and I'm like, "Okay, I'm on my way,

00:02:42.357 --> 00:02:43.190
"I'm on my way."

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:44.770
- Yeah.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.050
- You know, they're everything to me.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.010
- It's beautiful, that's beautiful.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:50.130
We know Coach O'Fallon loves his team

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:51.750
but they love him, too,

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.610
and wanted to tell him in person.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.948
Come on out, boys!

00:02:54.948 --> 00:02:58.818
(hollering, applause)

00:02:58.818 --> 00:03:01.327
Yeah!

00:03:01.327 --> 00:03:04.676
(whistling, clapping)

00:03:04.676 --> 00:03:05.906
- What's up, Coach?

00:03:05.906 --> 00:03:06.739
- Oh, no!

00:03:08.088 --> 00:03:08.921
- Oh, guys...

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:10.629
- What's going on?

00:03:10.629 --> 00:03:12.286
- Aww.

00:03:12.286 --> 00:03:15.144
(applause)

00:03:15.144 --> 00:03:17.477
(whistling)

00:03:19.244 --> 00:03:20.224
- Oh, no...

00:03:20.224 --> 00:03:21.057
- Hi Coach, how you doing?

00:03:21.057 --> 00:03:22.057
- Oh my God!

00:03:23.094 --> 00:03:24.174
- What's up, Coach?

00:03:24.174 --> 00:03:25.871
(clapping)

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:28.573
- Y'all are such great guys!

00:03:28.573 --> 00:03:30.760
Like, you ran out and hugged!

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.410
I hope my boys are like you.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:33.290
Okay.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.560
Tell Coach what he means to you.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.450
Why'd you want to be here?

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.940
Tell him what he means to you.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.750
- Ever since day one.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.910
We didn't have the best
patch at first, (laughs)

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.520
but we got to learn

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.070
and got real good with each other.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:45.903
At first, you know,

00:03:45.903 --> 00:03:47.290
how I wasn't the best at

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.220
taking criticism well (laughs) but...

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.765
- No teenager is, by the way,

00:03:50.765 --> 00:03:51.598
but we all were,

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:52.431
we all were you.

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:53.264
(laughter)

00:03:53.264 --> 00:03:54.097
- But he pushed me

00:03:54.097 --> 00:03:55.810
where I didn't think I could be pushed.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.200
Like, he seen that I had a lot

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.240
of potential in me,

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.120
and I didn't see it, at first,

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:00.953
and he just

00:04:00.953 --> 00:04:01.950
pushed me so hard, I,

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.160
first I, you know,

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.030
I didn't really like,

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.060
I was like,

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.240
well, this guy, new coach,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.030
he's trying to tell me
to do all this stuff.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:09.765
But it worked out all in the end,

00:04:09.765 --> 00:04:10.598
because--

00:04:10.598 --> 00:04:11.431
- He pushes you because
he believes in you,

00:04:11.431 --> 00:04:13.180
and he sees something that
you might not see, yet.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.013
- Yeah.

00:04:14.013 --> 00:04:14.846
- Yeah.

00:04:14.846 --> 00:04:15.679
So, has this,

00:04:15.679 --> 00:04:17.914
what do you admire about Coach O'Fallon?

00:04:17.914 --> 00:04:19.570
- He's always been like,

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:20.430
a great person.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:22.610
Even when he first came into the gym.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.380
I already noticed that he had a passion

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.640
for basketball, you know?

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:26.730
And the, most of the guys here

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.460
have a passion for the game, too,

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.330
and he's always been like a second father

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.163
to me.

00:04:31.163 --> 00:04:32.220
I always seen him as that.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.660
And then,

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.005
his diagnosis and stuff,

00:04:35.005 --> 00:04:36.330
it was kind of sad.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.163
There was days when he

00:04:37.163 --> 00:04:37.996
couldn't even,

00:04:37.996 --> 00:04:39.140
he couldn't even stand,

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.690
and he still managed to come in,

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:42.420
which is really amazing of him.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.900
And he's shown me that anything,

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:44.733
that you can,

00:04:44.733 --> 00:04:45.590
with dedication and hard work

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.184
you can overcome anything.

00:04:47.184 --> 00:04:50.253
(applause)

00:04:50.253 --> 00:04:52.142
- What does this mean to you?

00:04:52.142 --> 00:04:52.975
I mean, to make an impression

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:55.480
on teenagers

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.640
is already hard enough.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.234
And you've made an,

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.950
an extreme one.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.510
- Well, like I said earlier,

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:02.730
With these group here,

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.790
just these individuals right here,

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.270
they're so special to me.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:07.103
And

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.020
we, our motto, besides being one-and-oh,

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.070
is that we always talked about

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:12.500
being family.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.810
That's you know, they are, they,

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.130
till the day they go off

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:18.130
and venture off into
other parts of the world,

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:18.963
it's like that, they're always

00:05:18.963 --> 00:05:20.100
gonna be my family.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.430
They always know as long as I'm around,

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:23.970
they can always reach out to me,

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.140
and vice-versa.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.030
Matter of fact, it was so funny,

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.930
I was having to think about
you guys this weekend,

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:29.763
and I was just like,

00:05:29.763 --> 00:05:30.596
"I gotta text my guys,

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.163
"just to see how they're doing."

00:05:32.163 --> 00:05:34.387
(audience member coos)

00:05:34.387 --> 00:05:35.220
But they,

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.200
I mean, it's been an honor and a pleasure

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.450
to be a part of these,

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:40.099
these young men's lives.
- Yeah.

00:05:40.099 --> 00:05:43.038
(applause)

00:05:43.038 --> 00:05:44.598
Well,

00:05:44.598 --> 00:05:45.780
there's someone else here

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.010
who can't wait to meet Coach O'Fallon.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.237
Come on out, Kobe!

00:05:49.237 --> 00:05:50.476
(whooshing)

00:05:50.476 --> 00:05:52.917
(uproarious applause)

00:05:52.917 --> 00:05:55.186
(fanfare)

00:05:55.186 --> 00:05:58.353
(boisterous applause)

00:05:59.404 --> 00:06:00.654
- That's right!

00:06:02.214 --> 00:06:03.047
- Hi!

00:06:03.047 --> 00:06:03.880
How ya doing, Coach?

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.969
- It's a pleasure.

00:06:05.969 --> 00:06:06.802
- Oh, my gosh!

00:06:06.802 --> 00:06:08.746
- What's up, young man?

00:06:08.746 --> 00:06:09.579
What's up?

00:06:10.429 --> 00:06:11.829
What's up?

00:06:11.829 --> 00:06:14.345
What's up, man, how ya doing?

00:06:14.345 --> 00:06:15.217
What's up?

00:06:15.217 --> 00:06:18.514
Yo, what's going on, back here?

00:06:18.514 --> 00:06:19.347
What's happening?

00:06:19.347 --> 00:06:21.567
(applause)

00:06:21.567 --> 00:06:24.210
- Oh my gosh! (laughs)

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.043
I wish,

00:06:25.043 --> 00:06:25.876
wait, come on over here!

00:06:25.876 --> 00:06:27.281
Can y'all, you can sit right between.

00:06:27.281 --> 00:06:28.114
- All right.

00:06:28.114 --> 00:06:28.989
- Right here?

00:06:28.989 --> 00:06:29.822
- Oh my,

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:30.880
okay, I wish we had a slow, like,

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:32.750
motion camera on you, my man.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:34.187
He went, he heard me go,

00:06:34.187 --> 00:06:35.020
"Ko..."

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.167
and he went, "What?"

00:06:36.167 --> 00:06:37.110
(laughter)

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:37.943
He was like,

00:06:37.943 --> 00:06:39.170
he was so excited.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.853
What do you want to say to Coach O'Fallon?

00:06:40.853 --> 00:06:41.686
- I mean, it's just

00:06:41.686 --> 00:06:42.890
extremely inspirational,

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:43.890
when we talk about,

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.000
sometimes we get caught up

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.010
in the world of sports

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.190
and thinking about

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.010
the significance of each game,

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.636
but not understanding that the game is,

00:06:51.636 --> 00:06:54.450
pales in comparison to life.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.030
And the lessons that we teach as coaches,

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:57.980
and the inspirational message

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.100
that he's created for his players,

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.720
the determination, the fighting,

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.103
the belief,

00:07:03.103 --> 00:07:04.260
is something that's,

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.356
that's

00:07:05.356 --> 00:07:07.800
way more valuable than
anything that you can learn

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.030
from hitting the game-winning shot,

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.360
or winning the NBA championship,

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.560
or winning the high-school championship,

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.810
whatever the case may be.

00:07:13.654 --> 00:07:15.350
So it's just a true inspiration, man.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.255
- Thank you.

00:07:16.255 --> 00:07:17.088
- Any of y'all have any questions

00:07:17.088 --> 00:07:18.022
for Kobe, I'm just saying...

00:07:18.022 --> 00:07:19.833
(laughter)

00:07:19.833 --> 00:07:20.666
- Y'all caught me off guard.

00:07:20.666 --> 00:07:21.499
I was not--

00:07:21.499 --> 00:07:23.004
(laughter, clapping)

00:07:23.004 --> 00:07:23.933
Y'all told me Martha Stewart

00:07:23.933 --> 00:07:24.766
was gonna be here,

00:07:24.766 --> 00:07:25.599
it was like,

00:07:25.599 --> 00:07:26.774
you didn't say nothing about Kobe,

00:07:26.774 --> 00:07:27.607
come on.

00:07:27.607 --> 00:07:29.274
Got my hands sweaty.

00:07:30.254 --> 00:07:31.311
- "My hands are sweating!" (laughs)

00:07:31.311 --> 00:07:33.672
(applause)

00:07:33.672 --> 00:07:34.790
No, but here's the thing:

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.310
he started out just like y'all,

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:37.143
on a team,

00:07:37.143 --> 00:07:38.070
growing up playing ball,

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.140
and you never know where you,

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.985
I mean, I did the same thing in my field,

00:07:40.985 --> 00:07:42.130
you never know.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:43.170
It doesn't matter where you come from,

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:44.543
it doesn't matter how much money you have,

00:07:44.543 --> 00:07:46.410
that does not limit your dreams.

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:48.030
And you can accomplish anything.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.545
And it doesn't matter what's
going on, you can do it.

00:07:49.545 --> 00:07:51.193
(applause)

